{
 "_README": [
  "Veterinary indication -> condition area, for the drug-pairs filter (amendment A13).",
  "339 distinct indications, 206 appearing once, make a raw indication filter unusable.",
  "Ordered regexes, first match wins, so specific areas precede general ones: a mammary",
  "carcinoma is oncology, an orthopaedic surgery is musculoskeletal rather than anaesthesia.",
  "Patterns spell the ae digraph as a?e? so British and American spellings both match -",
  "an earlier version used [ae], which matched 'anesthesia' but not 'anaesthesia' and",
  "silently sent British spellings to 'other'.",
  "Display only: pair records are unchanged and the indication itself stays searchable."
